[Desktop Entry]
# The Linux counterpart of scripts/install-rn.cmd: the file that exists to be
# clicked. Double-clicking a .sh opens an editor on every desktop worth the
# name, so the clickable thing has to be a launcher that runs the script rather
# than the script itself.
#
# Exec carries no path into this repository on purpose. It fetches the
# installer over HTTPS and pipes it to bash with --from-release, so the same
# file works from a checkout, from a download, or copied to another machine
# that has never seen rn.
#
# What it fetches is install-gui.sh, not install.sh, and Terminal is therefore
# false: the install reports in dialogs — a confirmation, a progress window
# naming each step, and a result window offering to open rn or to show the
# log. install-gui.sh is a face over install.sh and decides nothing; it falls
# back to a terminal, and then to xmessage, on a machine with no zenity or
# kdialog, which is why dropping Terminal=true costs nothing. Its header says
# why the terminal stopped being the default.
#
# The `set -o pipefail` in Exec is load-bearing rather than tidiness: without
# it a curl that fails hands bash an empty script, bash exits 0, and the ||
# never fires — a double-click that does nothing at all, silently, which is
# the worst outcome this file can produce.
#
# The quoting in Exec is the desktop-entry spec's, not the shell's: only double
# quotes count, and space | ; ' are reserved characters that must sit inside
# them. Single quotes around the whole command — the obvious shell instinct —
# is rejected outright by desktop-file-validate.
#
# To use it: copy to ~/.local/share/applications/ and it appears in the menu,
# or to ~/Desktop and `chmod +x` it, which is what xfdesktop wants before it
# will launch a file rather than open it.
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=Install rn
GenericName=rn installer
Comment=Download the latest rn release and install it for this user
Exec=bash -c "set -o pipefail; curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PieterdenEngelse/rn/main/scripts/install-gui.sh | bash -s -- --from-release || zenity --error --title='Install rn' --text='Could not download the rn installer. Check the network, then try again.' || xmessage -center 'Could not download the rn installer. Check the network, then try again.'"
Icon=system-software-install
Terminal=false
Categories=System;
Keywords=rn;install;automation;
StartupNotify=true
